43
00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.933
And you can initialize the guard
to run around your AI LLM

44
00:02:32.933 --> 00:02:37.300
call on the input or output side.
And on fail action

45
00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:42.400
basically specifies how you want Guardrails
to handle any type of failure.

46
00:02:43.433 --> 00:02:46.300
So for example,
if you detect hallucinations,

47
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.966
do you want to block the LLM
for answering

48
00:02:48.966 --> 00:02:50.933
or do you want to just let it continue

49
00:02:50.933 --> 00:02:53.933
and then log on the back end
that that failure occurred.

50
00:02:54.166 --> 00:02:57.533
All of this can be configured
using the on fail actions class.

